Effective Sea-Level Angular Momentum Functions (SLAM)

File name                    : ESMGFZ_SLAM_v1.2_24h_2024.asc
File contents                : effective angular momentum functions from global sea-level mass balance
File units                   : dimensionless earth rotation excitation functions
Issue date                   : 2025-01-01
Version number               : v1.2
 
References                   : Dobslaw, H., R. Dill, A. Groetzsch, A. Brzezinski, and M. Thomas (2010), 
                               Seasonal polar motion excitation from numerical models of atmosphere, ocean, 
                               and continental hydrosphere, J. Geophys. Res., doi:10.1029/2009JB007127
 
Contact                      : Henryk Dobslaw, dobslaw@gfz-potsdam.de
Affiliation                  : Deutsches GeoForschungsZentrum GFZ
                               Dep. 1: Geodesy and Remote Sensing
                               Sec. 1.3: Earth System Modelling
                               Telegrafenberg
                               14473 Potsdam, Germany
 
Temporal domain              : 01.01.2024 through 31.12.2024 (12:00 UTC)
Temporal resolution          : 24h 
Number of data records       : 366
Subtracted mean value        : mean from 2003-01-01 to 2014-12-31 (only x-, y-, z-component mass terms)
                               2.069815068012571e-13   3.295849259181661e-13   2.508252140298746e-1
 
Sea-level                    : Global mass balance according to ECMWF op. surface pressure and
                               continental hydrology from Land Surface Discharge Model (LSDM)

Notes : These SLAMs are part of a set of consistently processed Earth rotation excitation 
        function (AAM, OAM, HAM, SLAM). The ocean model MPIOM and the hydrological model LSDM were
        forced consistently with operational forecast data from the ECMWF.
 
Further references to be mentioned, when LSDM data are used:
         Dill, R., Hydrological model LSDM for operational Earth rotation and gravity field variations.
                   GFZ Scientific Technical Report STR08/09, 2008

